  "title": "GENERATING PERSONAS USING MULTIMODAL DATA",
  "technical_field": "[0002] This disclosure relates generally to artificial intelligence (AI) systems, and more particularly to generating personas.",
  "background_art": "[0003] Artificial Intelligence (AI) can be used to generate synthetic content such as text, images, videos, etc., based on training datasets. For example, AI models may be trained to learn patterns within the training dataset so that they can predict what content will look like when given a prompt. However, there are limitations to current approaches. For instance, many existing methods require manual annotation which increases cost and time. Additionally, these methods do not capture all aspects of human behavior such as body language, tone, voice, etc.
[0004] In some cases, generative AI models have been developed to mimic certain aspects of humans. For example, generative adversarial networks (GANs) can generate realistic images, but these GANs typically focus only on visual appearance without considering other modalities such as speech. As another example, virtual assistants use natural language processing techniques to understand spoken commands, but these virtual assistants lack understanding of context and physical presence.
[0005] Accordingly, it would be beneficial to develop new methods and systems to improve the accuracy and efficiency of AI model generation while reducing costs and improving functionality.",
  "summary_of_invention": "[0010] According to various embodiments, this disclosure provides methods and apparatuses for generating a persona. An embodiment includes capturing, for each of a plurality of video frames, sensor data including image and audio of a subject. Image and/or audio data is extracted from the sensor data. First geometric data representing a geometry of the subject is determined using the image data. Audio data is converted into audio latents. Based on the audio latents, second geometric data representing the subject is determined using the audio latents. The second geometric data is different than the first geometric. A three-dimensional (3D) geometric representation of the subject for a subject persona (e.g., avatar) is generated using the second geometric data.
[0011] One advantage of some embodiments disclosed herein is improved performance. By utilizing multimodal data (i.e., both image and audio), embodiments can create more accurate representations of subjects than those created using single-modal data (e.g., either just image or just audio). Moreover, embodiments utilize unsupervised learning techniques, which reduce the need for costly annotations. Embodiments also provide for reduced latency compared to prior art approaches. Furthermore, embodiments enable the creation of avatars that reflect a person's personality, mood, and emotional state, providing a more immersive experience. Also, embodiments allow for real-time adaptation of avatars, enabling them to change their expressions, postures, and tones according to changing situations.
[0012] Another advantage of some embodiments disclosed herein is flexibility. Embodiments can operate across multiple platforms, including web browsers, mobile devices, desktop computers, head-mounted displays, augmented reality (AR) glasses, virtual reality (VR) goggles, and mixed reality (MR) helmets. These embodiments can work seamlessly regardless of whether users interact through touchscreens, controllers, keyboards, microphones, cameras, or any combination thereof. They can even adapt to varying lighting conditions, ensuring consistent quality in different environments.
[0013] Yet another advantage of some embodiments disclosed herein is scalability. Some embodiments can handle large-scale deployment in diverse settings, from small teams to massive enterprises. They can efficiently process vast amounts of user-generated content, adapting to changes in traffic volume and maintaining high-quality outputs under load.
[0014] Still yet another advantage of some embodiments disclosed herein is security. Embodiments employ robust encryption methods to protect sensitive information, safeguarding against unauthorized access and misuse. They maintain compliance with regulatory requirements, ensuring that personal data is handled responsibly. Embodiments also implement strict authentication protocols to verify identities, preventing impersonation attacks and protecting against malicious activities.
[0015] Other advantages of the present invention will become apparent upon reading the following description and appended claims, and upon reference to the accompanying drawings.",
